  </header>
  <main id="main-content">
    <section class="r5-hero" aria-labelledby="r5-title">
      <div class="r5-hero-copy"><p class="eyebrow">MII / SPATIAL COMPUTER</p><h1 id="r5-title">Work with Eve<br /><em>in your room.</em></h1><p class="lead">Ask Eve by voice, look at the result in the room, and point to what you want to change. This is the experience mii is being designed for.</p><div class="r5-hero-actions"><a class="button" href="#experience">Explore the idea <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a><a class="text-link" href="#status">See what is real today ↗</a></div><p class="hero-truth"><span aria-hidden="true"></span>Design and feasibility stage · No physical R5 accepted · No sales</p></div>
      <figure class="r5-hero-media"><img src="/images/avocadomini-r5-slim-home-concept.png" alt="Concept of a slim silver avocadoMini with a black sensor band and low dock beside a spatial call card" fetchpriority="high" /><figcaption>Concept visualization. The device, call, and floating display have not been built or validated.</figcaption></figure>
    </section>
    <section id="purpose" class="product-purpose" aria-labelledby="mini-purpose-title"><p class="eyebrow">WHY MINI / DAILY LIFE &amp; BETTER PLACES</p><h2 id="mini-purpose-title">For everyday life.<br />For the places we share.</h2><p>Mini is being designed to contribute to daily life and community-led place-making: helping people use their homes, shared facilities, and neighborhoods in ways that work for them.</p><div class="purpose-grid"><article><h3>At home.</h3><p>Explore simpler ways to control a room, communicate, create, and play through approved actions.</p></article><article><h3>In shared places.</h3><p>Explore guidance, learning, and play in community spaces, with accessible controls and a clear person responsible for each installation.</p></article><article><h3>Shape the neighborhood.</h3><p>Help residents share ideas about a place and discuss improvements together. The people who use the space should help decide what it does.</p></article></div><p class="purpose-note">These are proposed uses, not proven community outcomes. The Hub runs the room locally under the account holder’s permissions. Installations need consent, privacy controls, site-specific safety checks, and a manual fallback. No continuous resident tracking is assumed.</p></section>
    <section class="r5-intro" aria-labelledby="r5-intro-title"><p class="eyebrow">SPATIAL CORE</p><h2 id="r5-intro-title">How the room<br />sees and responds.</h2><p>The standard mii setup uses four Towers and a separate Hub. The Towers sense movement from different positions. The Hub runs RockstarOS, combines their inputs and sends the result to the display. A single Tower is planned for limited Eve interactions.</p><div class="r5-fact-row"><span>FOUR TOWERS</span><span>ONE HUB</span><span>REPLACEABLE DISPLAY</span></div></section>
    <section class="r5-form" aria-labelledby="r5-form-title"><figure><img src="/images/avocadomini-r5-slim-form-reference.png" alt="Design reference showing a slim silver cylindrical Mini with a black sensor band standing on a low round dock" loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Product-form reference, not final hardware or a measured production design.</figcaption></figure><div><p class="eyebrow">R5 FORM STUDY</p><h2 id="r5-form-title">The Tower head.</h2><p>The R5 cylinder is a design reference for the head of a Tower. The mounting depends on where the sensors need to see. The Hub can sit elsewhere in the room.</p><p class="r5-form-note">Optics, power, heat and installation remain under review.</p></div></section>
    <section id="experience" class="r5-experience" aria-labelledby="r5-experience-title"><div class="r5-section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">THE EXPERIENCE WE ARE TESTING</p><h2 id="r5-experience-title">A useful day,<br />not a fixed mode.</h2></div><div class="r5-experience-grid"><article><span>01 / LIVE</span><h3>Feel at home.</h3><p>Explore approved room actions and clear, reversible choices. Compatible devices and permissions must be confirmed first.</p></article><article><span>02 / MAKE</span><h3>Keep creating.</h3><p>Start an idea, review an Agent result, and keep the same work and its history as you move.</p></article><article><span>03 / PLAY</span><h3>Move into play.</h3><p>Use spatial input with a supported game. Game availability, sensing quality, and local performance need separate acceptance.</p></article><article><span>04 / RESUME</span><h3>Pick up your work.</h3><p>Return to a saved task through your account. Continuity across devices needs end-to-end testing.</p></article></div><p class="r5-experience-note">These are intended experiences, not features available on production hardware today.</p></section>
    <section class="r5-create-cta" aria-labelledby="r5-create-title"><div><p class="eyebrow">TAKE PART IN THE BUILD</p><h2 id="r5-create-title">Your next game<br />starts here.</h2><p>Try a browser game starter, make your own version, or send a product idea. The creator preview is open now; Mini hardware and game publication still require separate acceptance.</p></div><a class="button" href="/create/">Create games & send ideas ↗</a></section>
    <section id="design" class="r5-design" aria-labelledby="r5-design-title"><figure><img src="/images/avocadomini-r5-removable-dock-concept.png" alt="Concept showing a slim Mini being lifted from a reachable wall dock that stays in place" loading="lazy" /><figcaption>R5 removable dock study. The image illustrates one mounting idea.</figcaption></figure><div><p class="eyebrow">ROOM INSTALLATION</p><h2 id="r5-design-title">Position the Towers.</h2><p>The design allows wall, ceiling or column placements. The separate Hub processes their shared view. Placement, calibration and a reachable stop control must be tested in the actual room.</p><a class="text-link" href="#status">Read the development status ↗</a></div></section>
    <section class="r5-vision" aria-labelledby="r5-vision-title"><div><p class="eyebrow">THE LONGER VIEW</p><h2 id="r5-vision-title">Less screen.<br />More presence.</h2><p>Spatial call notices and hand input are part of the R5 design goal. A sensor alone cannot create a visible image or complete a phone call. Display optics, privacy, recognition, audio, a real network, and fallback controls must work together in the same tested setup.</p></div><div class="r5-vision-panel"><span>WHAT MUST BE PROVEN</span><ul><li>Readable and safe spatial output</li><li>Reliable input and owner verification</li><li>Real calls and portable connectivity</li><li>Account, Eve and Noah continuity</li></ul></div></section>
    <section id="status" class="r5-status" aria-labelledby="r5-status-title"><div class="r5-status-heading"><p class="eyebrow">DEVELOPMENT STATUS</p><h2 id="r5-status-title">A concept with<br />clear next steps.</h2><p>R5 requirements and experience are documented. No complete Mini prototype has passed the physical acceptance gates.</p></div><div class="r5-status-grid"><article><span>DESIGN</span><strong>In progress</strong><p>The Tower and Hub roles, display options and hardware acceptance criteria are documented.</p></article><article><span>PHYSICAL DEVICE</span><strong>Not accepted</strong><p>Display, sensing, calls, optional LTE connectivity, power, heat, and recovery have not passed together.</p></article><article><span>ROCKSTAROS ON MINI</span><strong>Not available</strong><p>No signed, recoverable Mini OS image or public Mini installer has been accepted.</p></article><article><span>SALES</span><strong>Closed</strong><p>No reservation, payment, final R5 price, or release date is available.</p></article></div><div class="r5-status-actions"><a class="button" href="/preorder/">Full status & next steps ↗</a><a class="text-link" href="/install/">Available Web preview & OS status ↗</a></div></section>
    <section class="r5-ecosystem" aria-labelledby="r5-ecosystem-title"><div><p class="eyebrow">CONNECTED BY DESIGN</p><h2 id="r5-ecosystem-title">One foundation.<br />Different hardware.</h2><p>RockstarOS runs on the Hub. Noah lets you choose an Agent and connect it to your Mac. Eve is where you request work and review results. avocadoPro is a separate AI-dedicated PC.</p></div><div class="r5-ecosystem-links"><a href="https://avoado.si/">Explore the avokado service <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a href="https://avocadopro.si/">Explore avocadoPro <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a href="/install/">Check RockstarOS access <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></section>
